{
  "findings": [
    {
      "fact": "NovaSQL is a managed PostgreSQL‑compatible relational database that stores data in tables with a fixed schema and supports relational joins, enabling transactional consistency.",
      "source": "novacloud_platform_docs.txt#9"
    },
    {
      "fact": "NovaDocument is a managed MongoDB‑compatible document database that stores flexible JSON‑like documents without a fixed schema and does not provide relational joins.",
      "source": "novacloud_platform_docs.txt#10"
    },
    {
      "fact": "NovaSQL automatically performs backups every six hours with configurable retention of 7‑35 days and supports point‑in‑time recovery, providing data protection for relational workloads.",
      "source": "novacloud_platform_docs.txt#9"
    },
    {
      "fact": "NovaDocument automatically distributes documents across storage nodes, providing horizontal scalability and high availability for document‑oriented data.",
      "source": "novacloud_platform_docs.txt#10"
    },
    {
      "fact": "The design choice for NovaSQL emphasizes strong ACID guarantees and relational query capabilities for transaction‑heavy applications, whereas NovaDocument prioritizes schema flexibility and easy scaling for unstructured data.",
      "source": "novacloud_platform_docs.txt#31"
    },
    {
      "fact": "Trade‑offs: NovaSQL’s relational model offers consistency and complex queries but requires provisioning of 1‑128 virtual CPUs and up to 1 TB of memory, while NovaDocument sacrifices join capabilities for flexible schema and automatic sharding, simplifying development of agile applications.",
      "source": "novacloud_platform_docs.txt#31"
    }
